#
# Source    : https://android.googleapis.com/attestation/root   (retrieved 2026-08-26)
# Reference : https://developer.android.com/privacy-and-security/security-key-attestation
#
# Reproduce and verify:
#   curl -s https://android.googleapis.com/attestation/root | jq -r '.[]' > roots.pem
#   openssl x509 -in this-file.pem -outform DER | openssl dgst -sha256
#   # expected: cedb1cb6dc896ae5ec797348bce9286753c2b38ee71ce0fbe34a9a1248800dfc
#
# Rotation: Google publishes new roots without notice (the Key Attestation CA1 root appeared in
# 2025). When a chain is rejected with "does not lead to a trusted root" and the device is genuine,
# re-fetch the source above and add the missing root here. A deployment that cannot wait for a
# release can set client_instance_platform_config.android_key_attestation.trusted_root_certificates
# on the client instead.
#
